## GEMM optimization (2026-07-06)
WHAT WE ARE WORKING ON: run GLM-5.2-MXFP4's dense projection linears — o_proj,
q_a, q_b — on the FP8 GEMM instead of bf16. They currently run hgemm_bf16
(MXFP4 weight dequant -> bf16, bf16 GEMM); route them onto the aiter FP8 CK
GEMM `gemm_a8w8_blockscale_bpreshuffle` (already in fp8_utils.py) that ATOM uses
for its dense projections.

OUT OF SCOPE (colleague's territory — do NOT touch): GLM MLA absorbed bmm in
fp8 (w_kc/w_vc), and switching decode to the aiter fp8 MLA decode kernel.

FORMAT (verified from amd/GLM-5.2-MXFP4 config.json): the MLA dense projections
(q_a_proj, q_b_proj, kv_a_proj_with_mqa, kv_b_proj, o_proj) are in the quark
`exclude` list for EVERY layer -> stored BF16, run via UnquantizedLinearMethod
-> tgemm.mm (hgemm_bf16). Only the MoE experts are fp4. So there is NO
MXFP4->FP8 bridge: the weights are already bf16.
PLAN: at load (process_weights_after_loading), block-quant the bf16 projection
weight -> FP8 e4m3 + 128x128 UE8M0 scales (fp8_utils.quant_weight_ue8m0) +
shuffle_weight for bpreshuffle; stash on layer. At apply, route through
aiter_w8a8_block_fp8_linear (activations quantized to FP8 at runtime via
aiter_per1x128_quant). Gated by an opt-in flag, gfx950 + these excluded MLA
projections only. Accuracy risk = bf16->FP8 weight + FP8 activation (ATOM ships
these projections in FP8, so precedent it holds); verify GSM8K.

RESULT (2026-07-06, SGLANG_DSA_FP8_PROJ_GEMM, e0d1a2f041): IMPLEMENTED +
validated on box (gfx950). q_b_proj/o_proj bf16 -> FP8 e4m3 block repack at
load (quant_weight_ue8m0 + shuffle_weight(16,16)); apply consumes the MLA
forward's (fp8_act, scale) tuple via aiter_w8a8_block_fp8_linear. Standalone
byte-compare cos>0.9994; GSM8K 1319 = 0.936 (no regression).
graph-ON decode A/B (8192/1024 TP4) vs canonical bf16 baseline:
