## DSA indexer fusion (2026-07-06) — the AttentionMLA lever that is OURS
Profile (GLM(GLM5.csv): AttentionMLA is the only real gap (15.5% overall).
Colleague owns the absorbed bmm + the fp8 MLA decode kernel; the part that is
OURS is the DSA indexer's fragmented kernels. On HIP/gfx950 the indexer runs
these SEPARATELY (profile, per layer): rope 9.16 + act_quant 5.78 +
indexer_k_quant_and_cache 5.80 + k-LayerNorm 5.51 (~26us) — because the fused
indexer mega-kernels (fused_q_indexer_rope_first_quant / fused_k_indexer_norm_
rope[_store]) are gated `if _is_cuda:` (dsa_indexer.py:166), NVIDIA-only.

LEVER: aiter's `indexer_qk_rope_quant_and_cache` fuses q-rope + q-fp8-quant +
k-norm + k-rope + k-fp8-quant + cache-store + weights-scale into ONE kernel.
CONFIRMED available in our aiter on the box (HAS_FUSED=True). ATOM enables it by
default on gfx950 (ATOM_ENABLE_DS_INDEXER_QK_ROPE_CACHE_FUSION=1). ATOM call
(atom/plugin/sglang/attention_backend/sparse_mla_indexer.py):
  indexer_qk_rope_quant_and_cache(q_bf16, q_fp8, weights, weights_out, k,
    kv_cache, slot_mapping, k_norm_weight, k_norm_bias, positions, cos_cache,
    sin_cache, k_norm_eps, quant_block_size, scale_fmt, weights_scale,
    preshuffle=preshuffle_cache, is_neox=is_neox_style)
PLAN: wire this into the indexer q/k prepare+store behind a flag (gfx950),
replacing the fragmented rope/norm/quant/store; validate byte-exact + GSM8K +
e2e_glm5.sh (TTFT + TPOT + throughput). Supersedes the standalone fused-rope +
FUSE_HADAMARD_QUANT (they become subsets of this one kernel).
